  "about": "The rule that turns the game's upper case menu text into the Title Case a window shows (owner decision 2026-11-24: Title Case, a short list of acronyms kept upper case). The launcher applies it to a row, section, tab or value that has no title of its own; a title in settings-ui.json always wins. The rule is the same in every language: a word is a run of letters and digits, with an apostrophe, a dot or a slash between two of them kept inside (3.1, DON'T, N/A, KM/H); everything else is a separator and is copied. Each word: (1) an entry of spellings (keyed by the upper case word) gives that exact text; (2) an entry of acronyms stays upper case; (3) a word with a slash is converted part by part; (4) a number with a unit: digits X gives x (4X, 0.75X, 16X9, 7680X4320), digits P gives p, digits M gives m, digits MS gives ms, digits HZ gives Hz, and any other word with a digit is kept as it is in upper case (4K, D3D12, PS5, 3.1); (5) a small word (small_words) is lower case unless it is the first or the last word of the text or follows a colon or an opening bracket; (6) any other word has its first letter in upper case and the rest in lower case. Input of any case gives the same result, and converting a result gives the result again.",
